                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2838635,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "So there are many species of maple tree, and they'll grow without fertilizer in areas where there's plenty of moisture in the soil.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 140.96501,
                  "from": 131.04501,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2838659,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "However, they'll only do this if another important criterion is fulfilled, which is that they must have full or partial sun exposure during the day and very cool nights.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 154.67,
                  "from": 141.365,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2838689,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "And I'll talk more about that in a minute. There are only certain parts of the world that provide all these conditions. One is Canada, and by that, I mean all parts of Canada, and the other is the Northeastern states of North America. In these areas, the climate suits the trees perfectly. In fact, Canada produces over two thirds of the world's maple syrup, which is why the five pointed maple leaf is a Canadian symbol and has featured on the flag since 1964.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2838690,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And I'll talk more about that in a minute.",
