                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2838835,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "As they were unable to keep the liquid for any length of time, they didn't have storage facilities in those days, they boiled the liquid by placing pieces of rock that had become scorching hot from the sun into the sap.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 232.575,
                  "from": 217.61499,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2838877,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "They did this until it turned into sugar, and they were then able to use this to sweeten their food and drinks.",
