            "content": "<h3><strong>Maple syrup</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>What is maple syrup?</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; made from the sap of the maple tree</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; added to food or used in cooking</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; colour described as <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_31\">______</span></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; very <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_32\">______</span> compared to refined sugar</p>\n<p><strong>The maple tree</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; has many species</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; needs sunny days and cool nights</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; maple leaf has been on the Canadian flag since 1964</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; needs moist soil but does not need fertiliser as well</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; best growing conditions and <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_33\">______</span> are in Canada and North America</p>\n<p><strong>Early maple sugar producers</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; made holes in the tree trunks</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; used hot&nbsp; <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_34\">______</span> to heat the sap</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; used tree bark to make containers for collection</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; sweetened food and drink with sugar</p>\n<p><strong>Today&rsquo;s maple syrup</strong></p>\n<p><em>The trees</em></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Tree trunks may not have the correct <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_35\">______</span> until they have been growing for 40 years.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; The changing temperature and movement of water within the tree produces the sap.</p>\n<p><em>The production</em></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; A tap drilled into the trunk and a <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_36\">______</span> carries the sap into a bucket.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Large pans of sap called evaporators are heated by means of a <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_37\">______</span> .</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; A lot of <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_38\">______</span> is produced during the evaporation process.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; &lsquo;Sugar sand&rsquo; is removed because it makes the syrup look <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_39\">______</span> and affects the taste.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; The syrup is ready for use.</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; A huge quantity of sap is needed to make a <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_40\">______</span> of maple syrup.</p>",
